{"id": "cloud-fish", "ids": "⿰魚雲", "title": "Cloud Fish", "pronunciation": "yún", "bopomofo": "ㄩㄣˊ", "meaning": "Fish that swim through clouds; metaphorically, elusive dreams or unattainable desires", "formation": "associative", "definitions": [{"zh": "游於雲中之魚，傳說中飛躍雲霄之靈物", "en": "Fish that swim in clouds; legendary creatures that leap through the sky"}, {"zh": "比喻難以捕捉之事物，虛幻縹緲之願望", "en": "Metaphor for elusive things, ethereal and ungraspable desires"}, {"zh": "指高遠不可及之理想", "en": "Lofty and unattainable ideals"}], "etymology": "In ancient cosmology, fish were earthbound creatures of water while clouds belonged to the celestial realm. This character should have emerged to describe the impossible union of these elements — creatures that transcend their nature to swim in sky-streams. Such a character would have captured the Chinese literary imagination's fascination with boundary-crossing and transformation.", "source": {"work": "《說文解字》", "gloss": "⿰魚雲，雲中游魚也。王問切。"}, "components": [{"char": "魚", "meaning": "fish"}, {"char": "雲", "meaning": "cloud"}], "examples": [{"text": "莊生夢中見⿰魚雲翱翔於九霄之上，醒來歎其不可得也。", "translation": "In Zhuangzi's dream, he saw cloud fish soaring above the nine heavens, and upon waking, sighed that they were unattainable.", "style": "classical"}, {"text": "詩人常以⿰魚雲喻指那些美好卻虛無的理想。", "translation": "Poets often use cloud fish as a metaphor for beautiful yet insubstantial ideals.", "style": "contemporary"}], "related": [{"char": "鯤", "pinyin": "kūn", "gloss": "legendary giant fish"}, {"char": "霓", "pinyin": "ní", "gloss": "rainbow, ethereal phenomena"}, {"char": "鸞", "pinyin": "luán", "gloss": "mythical bird"}], "tags": ["mythology", "transcendence", "dreams", "nature"], "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\">\n<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif+TC:wght@400;700&display=swap\");</style>\n<g transform=\"translate(12.57,62.39) scale(0.272798,0.430246) translate(-100.